    <div class="form-grp mb4"><label class="form-label">Content <span class="fs11 muted">— Markdown supported</span></label><textarea class="form-input" style="min-height:400px;padding:14px 16px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.8;font-family:var(--f)" placeholder="Write your knowledge page content here..."># Architecture Decision Records

## ADR-001: Hybrid Java + Python Architecture
**Date:** 2026-05-01 · **Status:** Accepted

### Context
The system needs both traditional project management (CRUD, workflows, RBAC) and AI capabilities (LLM analysis, RAG indexing, risk prediction).

### Decision
- **Java (Spring Boot 3.3)** for core business logic
- **Python (FastAPI + Celery)** for AI computation
- **Supabase (PostgreSQL)** as unified data layer
- **RabbitMQ** for async messaging between Java and Python

### Rationale
Java provides type safety and mature ecosystem for enterprise workflows. Python has the best LLM/NLP library support. Separating them allows independent scaling.

### Consequences
- Two deployment artifacts to manage
- gRPC bridge needed for synchronous calls
- All async communication via RabbitMQ

---

## ADR-002: UUID v7 for Primary Keys
**Date:** 2026-05-03 · **Status:** Accepted

### Context
UUID v4 (random) causes B-tree page splits in PostgreSQL, degrading write performance.

### Decision
Use UUID v7 (time-ordered) for all primary keys, stored as PG's native UUID type (16 bytes).

### Consequences
- 7.6x write throughput improvement over UUID v4
- Time-sortable keys enable efficient range queries
- 75% index size reduction vs VARCHAR(64)
</textarea></div>
