<div class="cb"><div class="detail-layout">
<div class="detail-hd">
  <div class="detail-id">AIPM-42</div>
  <div class="detail-title">Fix login page layout on mobile devices — sidebar collapse & responsive stacking</div>
  <div class="detail-meta">
    <span class="tag tag-hi">Bug</span><span class="tag tag-hi">High</span>
    <span class="muted">Created by Alice · Jun 3</span>
    <span class="muted">Updated 3 hours ago</span>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="detail-body">
  <div>
    <div class="card mb4"><div class="card-hd"><h3>Description</h3></div><div class="card-bd detail-desc">
      <p>The login page layout breaks on mobile viewports (&lt; 768px):</p>
      <ol style="padding-left:20px;margin:8px 0">
        <li>Sidebar is hidden but left panel still takes space</li>
        <li>Form inputs overflow the card width</li>
        <li>Brand panel should stack above the form, not beside it</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt4">Expected: Full-width centered card with brand logo above. Sidebar hidden. Form inputs constrained to card width.</p>
    </div></div>

    <div class="card mb4"><div class="card-hd"><h3>Comments</h3></div><div class="card-bd nopad">
      <div class="hover-row"><div class="flex items-center gap2 mb4"><div class="av">A</div><div><span class="fw6 fs13">Alice</span><span class="fs11 muted ml-2">2 days ago</span></div></div><p class="fs13" style="line-height:1.6">I can reproduce on Chrome 125, iPhone SE viewport. The flex layout is causing the sidebar's hidden width to still affect the content area.</p></div>
      <div class="hover-row"><div class="flex items-center gap2 mb4"><div class="av">B</div><div><span class="fw6 fs13">Bob</span><span class="fs11 muted ml-2">1 day ago</span></div></div><p class="fs13" style="line-height:1.6">Suggested fix: use <code class="mono fs12" style="background:hsl(var(--sf-h));padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px">@media (max-width: 768px)</code> to hide sidebar and make content full-width. I can pair on this.</p></div>
    </div></div>

    <div class="card"><div class="card-hd"><h3>Activity</h3></div><div class="card-bd nopad">
      <div class="hover-row fs12 muted">Alice changed status from <strong>To Do</strong> → <strong>In Progress</strong> · Jun 4</div>
      <div class="hover-row fs12 muted">Bob added a comment · Jun 4</div>
      <div class="hover-row fs12 muted">Alice created this issue · Jun 3</div>
    </div></div>
  </div>

  <div class="detail-sidebar">
    <div class="card mb4"><div class="card-hd"><h3>Details</h3></div><div class="card-bd" style="padding:12px 14px">
      <div class="side-item"><div class="side-label">Assignee</div><div class="flex items-center gap2"><div class="av">A</div><span class="fs13">Alice</span></div></div>
      <div class="side-item"><div class="side-label">Status</div><span class="tag tag-b">In Progress</span></div>
      <div class="side-item"><div class="side-label">Priority</div><span class="tag tag-hi">High</span></div>
      <div class="side-item"><div class="side-label">Story Points</div><span class="fs13 fw6">8</span></div>
      <div class="side-item"><div class="side-label">Sprint</div><span class="fs13">Sprint 3</span></div>
      <div class="side-item"><div class="side-label">Created</div><span class="fs12 muted">Jun 3, 2026</span></div>
    </div></div>

    <!-- ★ AI Issue Analysis Inline ★ -->
    <div class="card ai-glow mb4"><div class="card-hd"><div class="flex items-center gap2"><span class="pulse"></span><h3 class="brand">AI Analysis</h3></div></div><div class="card-bd fs12" style="line-height:1.6">
      <p class="mb4"><strong class="pri">Risk Score:</strong> <span class="fw6 brand" style="font-size:18px">32/100</span> <span class="tag tag-lo">Low</span></p>
      <p class="mb4"><strong class="pri">Root Cause:</strong> This bug stems from the split-panel flex layout approach chosen for v2.3 auth pages. The sidebar's <code class="mono" style="background:hsl(var(--sf-h));padding:1px 3px;border-radius:2px">w-[440px]</code> is not responsive.</p>
      <p class="mb4"><strong class="pri">Suggested Fix:</strong> Replace the split-panel with a centered card layout on mobile via <code class="mono" style="background:hsl(var(--sf-h));padding:1px 3px;border-radius:2px">@media</code> query. Remove hardcoded widths.</p>
      <p class="muted fs11" style="border-top:1px solid hsl(var(--e-d));padding-top:8px;margin-top:12px">Analyzed by Claude · Confidence: 92%</p>
    </div></div>
  </div>
</div>
</div></div></div>

